# Sennheiser TeamConnect Bar Driver (SSCv2, OpenAPI 1.16)
#
# Controls a Sennheiser TeamConnect Bar S or TeamConnect Bar M, the
# all-in-one video bars (4K camera, beamforming microphone array, stereo
# speakers), over Sennheiser Sound Control Protocol v2 (SSCv2): a REST API
# over HTTPS on port 443, JSON bodies, HTTP Basic authentication as the fixed
# user "api" with the third-party password set in the bar's Local Web UI,
# DeviceHub or Sennheiser Control Cockpit.
#
# Protocol reference (the manufacturer's own):
#   - "TCBar 3rd-party API", OpenAPI 1.16 (released 2026-07-06), the file the
#     Sennheiser 3rd Party API site's TC Bar Swagger page renders
#     (source_url below). One document covers both bars. This is the
#     defining document for every path, field, range, enumeration and status
#     code here. Archived in the workspace as
#     driver-roadmap/reference-docs/sennheiser-tcbar-openapi-1.16.yaml.
#   - "Sennheiser 3rd Party API" v6.2 (08/2026): the SSCv2 specification 2.3
#     (subscriptions, notification syntax) and the TC Bar known issues.
#     docs.cloud.sennheiser.com/en-us/api-docs/
#   - TeamConnect Bar instruction manual (07/2026), for what differs between
#     the S and the M and for the standby modes.
#
# Not hardware-verified: built from the documents above and checked against
# the simulator below. What the documents leave open is listed in the
# workspace record (driver-roadmap/shipped/sennheiser_tcbar.md).
#
# One driver for both bars: the S and the M share one OpenAPI document and
# every path in it. What differs is a value's range, not the command surface:
# the camera's zoom ceiling (per model and device profile), the Split network
# mode (Bar M only), and the PoE direction (the S is powered over its one
# Ethernet port; the M can power an extension microphone).
#
# Push, not polling (SSCv2 spec, "SSCv2 subscriptions"):
#   The bar streams every change of a subscribed resource as a Server-Sent
#   Event. GET /api/ssc/state/subscriptions opens the stream, the reply's
#   Content-Location header (and the "open" event) names the session, and a
#   PUT of a resource-path list to /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{id}/add
#   arms it. The bar then sends the current value of every listed resource
#   and each later change, whether it came from the remote control, Control
#   Cockpit, the Local Web UI or the API. The push block's register list
#   runs once per (re)open, so a reopen (the bar's "close" event, a dropped
#   stream, 300 s of silence) is also a full resync.
#
#   The subscription is one request per resource group: the bar refuses a
#   whole list when one path in it is unknown to its firmware, so a group
#   the firmware lacks costs only that group. Device state, mute and volume
#   are in groups of their own.
#
#   Polling (30 s) reads the few resources whose bodies can be told apart
#   without their path (device state, identify, firmware, naming, volume,
#   user interaction), as the liveness baseline. Everything else is read
#   from the stream only: a bare {"enabled": ..} or {"gain": ..} body says
#   nothing about which resource it is, and the seven-band equalizers, zone
#   lists and Dante lists are arrays.
#
#   The talker position (beam angle and which microphone the mixer selected)
#   and the level meters are FastResource feeds the spec says to subscribe
#   only while the data is in use: "Report Talker Position" and "Report
#   Level Meters" arm them on connect, and the Talker Position On/Off and
#   Meters On/Off commands switch them at runtime. Both are throttled to
#   five updates a second per value, and the newest value in each window is
#   written when it ends, so a talker's final position always lands. Both
#   relay to the cloud at low priority.
#
# Why YAML:
#   Everything on the wire is JSON over HTTPS with Basic auth, and the push
#   block's session handshake (platform 0.34.0) is the subscription
#   mechanism, so nothing needs code. The TeamConnect Ceiling Medium driver
#   is the same protocol in Python, written before the handshake was
#   declarative.
#
# Scope: every resource the TC Bar OpenAPI 1.16 declares except the raw
# address tree (/api/ssc/schema), the open-source licence download, 802.1X
# configuration (certificates and secrets, a network-commissioning task), the
# network interface list (its entries depend on the network mode and carry
# no fixed position), the Bluetooth device list, and the deprecated
# resources that have a replacement (/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/mute,
# /api/audio/outputs/dante and the four deprecated camera fields). The
# deprecated PoE output switch has no replacement, so it is read, never
# written. The PUTs Sennheiser's known-issues page calls dead (HDMI output,
# camera enable, video parameters, the Dante interface) are not in OpenAPI
# 1.16 and are read-only here.

id: sennheiser_tcbar
name: Sennheiser TeamConnect Bar
manufacturer: Sennheiser
category: video
version: 1.0.1
# Computed by the contract check: a device setting's `map` (the JSON
# true / false the bar expects for a boolean) arrived in 0.37.0.
min_platform_version: "0.37.0"
author: OpenAVC
description: >
  TeamConnect Bar S and Bar M video bars over SSCv2, the HTTPS REST API with
  Server-Sent Events. Microphone mute, speaker volume, camera framing (auto
  framing, person tiling, pan, tilt, zoom, the stored preset), microphone and
  speaker equalizers, exclusion and priority zones, noise gate and
  suppression, Dante extension inputs, Bluetooth, LED ring, standby mode and
  the bar's own warnings. Talker position and level meters are opt-in feeds.
  Every change streams in as it happens.

source_url: https://docs.cloud.sennheiser.com/en-us/api-docs/api-docs/open-api-tc-bar.html
tags: [sennheiser, teamconnect, tc-bar, video-bar, conferencing, camera, beamforming, dante, sscv2]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [sscv2]
ports: [443]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Sennheiser
    models:
      - TeamConnect Bar S
      - TeamConnect Bar M
      - TC Bar S
      - TC Bar M
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Built from Sennheiser's SSCv2 specification and the TC Bar OpenAPI
      1.16 schema, which covers both bars. Not yet run against a bar. The
      camera's zoom position goes to 500 on the Bar M (150 in the Microsoft
      Teams profile) and to 300 on the Bar S (400 in the Zoom profile, 200
      in Microsoft Teams). The Split network mode exists only on the Bar M.

help:
  overview: >
    Controls a Sennheiser TeamConnect Bar S or Bar M. Mute the microphones,
    set the speaker volume, switch the camera between auto framing, person
    tiling and a manual view, move and zoom it, and recall its stored
    preset. Commissioning settings (equalizers, exclusion and priority
    zones, noise gate, Dante extension microphones, LED ring, standby) are
    under Device Settings. The bar's own warnings (lens cap on, overheating, a failed
    camera or microphone) show as on/off values a trigger can watch.
    Everything the bar changes, from its remote, Control Cockpit or its web
    page, shows up here as it happens.
  setup: >
    1. Open the bar's Local Web UI (https:// and its IP address), DeviceHub
       or Sennheiser Control Cockpit, and go to Access & Security (Control
       Cockpit: Devices > TC Bar > Access).
    2. Under 3rd Party Access, turn access on and set a password: at least
       ten characters with a lowercase letter, a capital, a number and a
       symbol.
    3. Enter the bar's IP address and that password here. The user name is
       always "api".
    4. Turn on "Report Talker Position" if a macro follows who is talking,
       and "Report Level Meters" if a panel shows levels. Both are
       continuous feeds, so they stay off unless needed.
  connection: >
    HTTPS on port 443 with the third-party password. The bar's own
    certificate is self-signed, so certificate verification is off unless
    you turn it on. Turning third-party access off on the bar deletes the
    password; set a new one here after turning it back on.

discovery:
  # /api/device/identity answers without credentials (its OpenAPI entry
  # declares no security), and only a TC Bar answers with a product code
  # starting TCBar. HTTPS only, self-signed, so the probe is a TLS GET.
  tcp_probe:
    port: 443
    tls: true
    send_ascii: "GET /api/device/identity HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: tcbar\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
    expect_regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"TCBar[SM]"'
    extract_manufacturer: "Sennheiser"
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"(TCBar[SM])"'
        group: 1
  # Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG (IEEE registry).
  oui:
    - "00:1b:66"
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "sennheiser"

transport: http

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 443
  ssl: true
  verify_ssl: false
  auth_type: "basic"
  username: "api"
  password: ""
  timeout: 5.0
  poll_interval: 30
  enable_talker_position: false
  enable_meters: false

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
    help: "The bar's IP address, as shown in Control Cockpit or on its Local Web UI."
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 443
    label: HTTPS Port
    advanced: true
    help: "443 on every bar; change it only behind a port forward."
  password:
    type: string
    secret: true
    required: true
    label: Third-party Password
    help: >
      The 3rd Party Access password set under Access & Security on the bar.
      The user name is always "api" and needs no entry.
  verify_ssl:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Verify TLS Certificate
    advanced: true
    help: >
      Off by default: the bar ships a self-signed certificate. Turn on only
      if a trusted certificate has been installed on it.
  enable_talker_position:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Report Talker Position
    help: >
      Streams the microphone beam's angle and which microphone the mixer
      picked (the bar's own, or a Dante extension) as people talk, for a
      macro that follows the talker. Off by default because it is a
      continuous feed; the Talker Position On/Off commands also switch it.
  enable_meters:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Report Level Meters
    help: >
      Streams the microphone, USB, Bluetooth and Dante input levels. Off by
      default because it is a continuous feed; the Meters On/Off commands
      also switch it.

# ── Push: the SSCv2 subscription session ──────────────────────────────
# One stream, named by the bar; the register list arms it on every
# (re)open, one group per request so a group the firmware refuses costs
# only itself.
push:
  type: sse
  path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions
  # The bar documents no keepalive. A reopen after five quiet minutes is a
  # new session the bar answers with every value, so a quiet room gets a
  # free full resync and a half-open stream is noticed.
  idle_timeout: 300
  session:
    header: Content-Location
    event: open
    key: sessionUUID
    pattern: "([0-9a-fA-F-]{36})$"
    close_event: close
  register:
    - subscribe_device
    - subscribe_audio
    - subscribe_audio_processing
    - subscribe_equalizers
    - subscribe_zones
    - subscribe_dante_inputs
    - subscribe_camera
    - subscribe_device_settings
    - subscribe_network
    - subscribe_poe_output
    - { command: talker_position_on, when: enable_talker_position }
    - { command: meters_on, when: enable_meters }
  unregister: end_subscription

quick_actions: [identify_on]
actions:
  - id: mute_on
    icon: mic-off
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.mute", operator: falsy }
  - id: mute_off
    icon: mic
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.mute", operator: truthy }
  - id: volume_down
    icon: volume-1
  - id: volume_up
    icon: volume-2
  - id: identify_on
    icon: eye
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.identify_active", operator: falsy }
  - id: identify_off
    icon: eye-off
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.identify_active", operator: truthy }
  - id: open_web_ui
    kind: link
    label: Open Web UI
    icon: external-link

state_variables:
  # ── Identity ──
  product:
    type: string
    label: Product Code
    help: "TCBarS or TCBarM, as the bar identifies itself"
  model:
    type: string
    label: Model
  article_number:
    type: string
    label: Article Number
  serial:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
  hardware_revision:
    type: string
    label: Hardware Revision
  vendor:
    type: string
    label: Vendor
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "Set in Control Cockpit or the Local Web UI; read-only on this API"
  dante_name:
    type: string
    label: Dante Device Name
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
  position:
    type: string
    label: Position
  ssc_protocol_version:
    type: string
    label: SSC Protocol Version
  ssc_schema_version:
    type: string
    label: API Schema Version

  # ── Device state ──
  device_state:
    type: enum
    values: ["Normal", "Identifying", "BluetoothPairing", "FirmwareUpdate", "Standby", "CriticalFailure"]
    label: Device State
    help: "Standby is the bar's energy-saving state; it still answers on the network"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_count:
    type: integer
    label: Warnings
    help: "How many warnings the bar reports right now"
  warning_mic_muted:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Microphones Muted"
  warning_lens_cap_on:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Lens Cap On"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_camera_off:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Camera Off"
  warning_speaker_muted:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Speaker Muted"
  warning_no_device_connected:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: No Device Connected"
    help: "Nothing is connected over USB-C to run the call"
  warning_overheating:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Overheating"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_cpu_overloaded:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: CPU Overloaded"
  warning_bluetooth_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Bluetooth Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_dante_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Dante Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_mic_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Microphone Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_speaker_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Speaker Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_voice_engine_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Voice Engine Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_camera_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Camera Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_usb_failure:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: USB Failure"
    cloud_priority: high
  warning_time_uninitialized:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Clock Not Set"
    help: "The bar's clock is not set"
  warning_network_loop:
    type: boolean
    label: "Warning: Network Loop Detected"
    cloud_priority: high
  identify_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Identify
    help: "True while the bar's LEDs flash to show which unit this is"
  user_interaction:
    type: boolean
    label: User Interaction
    help: "The bar reports someone is using it"
    cloud_priority: high
  device_profile:
    type: enum
    values: ["Custom", "Zoom", "MicrosoftTeams"]
    label: Device Profile
    help: "Custom, or the Zoom or Microsoft Teams profile, which limit the camera"
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Version
  update_state:
    type: enum
    values: ["Idle", "Updating"]
    label: Firmware Update
    cloud_priority: high
  update_progress:
    type: integer
    label: Firmware Update Progress
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
  update_last_status:
    type: enum
    values: ["None", "ServerUnreachable", "DownloadFailed", "SignatureFailed", "DowngradeProhibited", "UpdateFailed"]
    label: Last Firmware Update Result
  standby_mode:
    type: enum
    values: ["AlwaysOn", "EcoMode", "LowPowerMode"]
    label: Standby Mode
  led_brightness:
    type: integer
    label: LED Brightness
    min: 0
    max: 5
  sound_prompts:
    type: boolean
    label: Sound Prompts
    help: "The bar's sound prompts. The welcome sound plays at every boot regardless"
  poe_output_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: PoE Output
    help: "Whether the bar supplies power over Ethernet to a connected device"

  # ── Network ──
  port_configuration:
    type: enum
    values: ["SingleDomain", "Split", "DualDomain"]
    label: Network Mode
    help: "Split is Bar M only. Set in Control Cockpit or the Local Web UI"
  wifi_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Wi-Fi
  wifi_connected:
    type: boolean
    label: Wi-Fi Connected
  wifi_ssid:
    type: string
    label: Wi-Fi Network
  wifi_signal:
    type: integer
    label: Wi-Fi Signal
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
  wifi_band:
    type: string
    label: Wi-Fi Band
  bluetooth_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Bluetooth
    control: true
  bluetooth_pairing:
    type: boolean
    label: Bluetooth Pairing
    help: "Pairing stays open for three minutes or until a device connects"
  bluetooth_mac:
    type: string
    label: Bluetooth Address
  dante_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Dante
    help: "Whether Dante is turned on; set in Control Cockpit or the Local Web UI"
  dante_continuous_stream:
    type: boolean
    label: Continuous Dante Stream
  dante_speaker_output:
    type: boolean
    label: Dante Speaker Output

  # ── Audio ──
  mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Microphone Mute
    help: "Mutes the bar's microphone and any Dante extension microphones"
    control: true
    cloud_priority: high
  volume:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker Volume
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
    control: true
  speaker_level_limit:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker Volume Limit
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
  mic_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Internal Microphone
  mic_gain_db:
    type: integer
    label: Internal Microphone Gain
    min: -60
    max: 0
    unit: dB
  noise_gate_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Noise Gate
  noise_gate_threshold_db:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Threshold
    min: -70
    max: -30
    unit: dB
  noise_gate_hold_ms:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Hold Time
    min: 100
    max: 500
    unit: ms
  noise_gate_range_db:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Range
    min: -80
    max: 0
    unit: dB
  noise_suppression:
    type: enum
    values: ["Low", "Medium", "High"]
    label: Noise Suppression
  sound_profile:
    type: enum
    values: ["Wallmount", "TableTop", "AboveDisplay", "UnderDisplay", "FreeStanding", "Custom"]
    label: Sound Profile
  mixer_fade:
    type: enum
    values: ["Slow", "Medium", "Fast"]
    label: Mic Selector Fade
  conference_out_far_end_db:
    type: integer
    label: Conference Output Far End Gain
    min: -60
    max: 0
    unit: dB
  conference_out_near_end_db:
    type: integer
    label: Conference Output Near End Gain
    min: -60
    max: 0
    unit: dB
  dante_input_1_gain_db:
    type: integer
    label: Dante Input 1 Gain
    min: -60
    max: 0
    unit: dB
  dante_input_2_gain_db:
    type: integer
    label: Dante Input 2 Gain
    min: -60
    max: 0
    unit: dB

  # Seven-band custom equalizers, lowest band first
  mic_eq_1:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 1 (lowest)
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  mic_eq_2:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 2
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  mic_eq_3:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 3
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  mic_eq_4:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 4
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  mic_eq_5:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 5
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  mic_eq_6:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 6
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  mic_eq_7:
    type: integer
    label: Mic EQ Band 7 (highest)
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_1:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 1 (lowest)
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_2:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 2
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_3:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 3
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_4:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 4
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_5:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 5
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_6:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 6
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB
  speaker_eq_7:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker EQ Band 7 (highest)
    min: -8
    max: 8
    unit: dB

  # Beam zones (degrees across the bar's pickup area, 15 to 165)
  exclusion_zone_1_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 1
  exclusion_zone_1_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Active
    help: "Sound is arriving from inside the zone right now"
  exclusion_zone_1_left:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Left Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  exclusion_zone_1_right:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Right Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  exclusion_zone_2_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 2
  exclusion_zone_2_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Active
    help: "Sound is arriving from inside the zone right now"
  exclusion_zone_2_left:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Left Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  exclusion_zone_2_right:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Right Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  exclusion_zone_3_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 3
  exclusion_zone_3_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Active
    help: "Sound is arriving from inside the zone right now"
  exclusion_zone_3_left:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Left Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  exclusion_zone_3_right:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Right Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  priority_zone_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Priority Zone
  priority_zone_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Priority Zone Active
    help: "Sound is arriving from inside the zone right now"
  priority_zone_gain:
    type: enum
    values: ["Low", "Medium", "High"]
    label: Priority Zone Gain
  priority_zone_left:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Left Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
  priority_zone_right:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Right Edge
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"

  # ── Talker position feed (opt-in) ──
  beam_azimuth:
    type: integer
    label: Talker Azimuth
    help: "The microphone beam's angle across the bar's pickup area, 15 to 165 degrees"
    min: 15
    max: 165
    unit: "°"
    cloud_priority: low
  active_mic:
    type: enum
    values: ["InternalMic", "ExternalMic1", "ExternalMic2"]
    label: Active Microphone
    help: "The microphone the bar's mixer has selected: its own, or Dante input 1 or 2"
    cloud_priority: low

  # ── Level meters (opt-in) ──
  max_peak_db:
    type: integer
    label: Loudest Input Level
    min: -60
    max: 10
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low
  mic_peak_db:
    type: integer
    label: Microphone Level
    min: -60
    max: 10
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low
  usb_level_db:
    type: integer
    label: USB Input Level
    min: -60
    max: 10
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low
  bluetooth_level_db:
    type: integer
    label: Bluetooth Input Level
    min: -60
    max: 10
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low
  dante_input_1_level_db:
    type: integer
    label: Dante Input 1 Level
    min: -60
    max: 10
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low
  dante_input_2_level_db:
    type: integer
    label: Dante Input 2 Level
    min: -60
    max: 10
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low

  # ── Camera ──
  camera_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Camera Active
    help: "The camera is streaming to the connected computer"
  autoframing:
    type: boolean
    label: Auto Framing
    control: true
  person_tiling:
    type: boolean
    label: Person Tiling
    control: true
  autoframing_button_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Remote Auto Framing Button
  person_tiling_button_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Remote Person Tiling Button
  camera_pan:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Pan
    min: -25
    max: 25
    control: true
  camera_tilt:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Tilt
    min: -25
    max: 25
    control: true
  camera_zoom:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Zoom
    help: "100 is no zoom. Bar M up to 500 (150 in the Microsoft Teams profile); Bar S up to 300 (400 in the Zoom profile, 200 in Microsoft Teams)"
    min: 100
    max: 500
    control: true
  camera_zoom_speed:
    type: enum
    values: ["Slow", "Medium", "Fast"]
    label: Remote Zoom Speed
  camera_pan_tilt_speed:
    type: enum
    values: ["Slow", "Medium", "Fast"]
    label: Remote Pan and Tilt Speed
  autoframing_speed:
    type: enum
    values: ["Slow", "Medium", "Fast"]
    label: Auto Framing Speed
  hdmi_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: HDMI Output
    help: "Set in Control Cockpit or the Local Web UI; the Microsoft Teams profile turns it off"
  camera_compensation:
    type: enum
    values: ["Off", "Backlight", "Lowlight"]
    label: Camera Light Compensation
  camera_anti_flicker:
    type: enum
    values: ["Auto", "50Hz", "60Hz", "Off"]
    label: Camera Anti-Flicker
  camera_brightness:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Brightness
    min: -12
    max: 12
  camera_contrast:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Contrast
    min: 1
    max: 10
  camera_saturation:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Saturation
    min: 0
    max: 10
  camera_sharpness:
    type: integer
    label: Camera Sharpness
    min: 0
    max: 6
  camera_auto_white_balance:
    type: boolean
    label: Camera Auto White Balance
  camera_white_balance_k:
    type: integer
    label: Camera White Balance
    min: 2800
    max: 6500
    unit: K
  camera_default_mode:
    type: enum
    values: ["ResumeLastView", "FullFieldOfView", "AutoFraming", "PersonTiling", "UserPreset"]
    label: Camera Mode at Call Start

# ── Device settings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Room setup the bar stores and reports back over the stream. Every write is
# a partial body (one field); the schema marks no field of these resources
# required. A boolean is written as the JSON literal the bar expects.
device_settings:
  mic_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Internal Microphone
    help: "Turns the bar's own microphone on or off; Dante extension microphones keep working"
    state_key: mic_enabled
    default: true
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic
      body: '{"enabled": {value}}'
  mic_gain_db:
    type: integer
    label: Internal Microphone Gain
    help: "-60 to 0 dB."
    state_key: mic_gain_db
    default: 0
    min: -60
    max: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic
      body: '{"gain": {value}}'
  speaker_level_limit:
    type: integer
    label: Speaker Volume Limit
    help: "Caps the speaker volume, in percent: at 50 the bar plays no louder than 50% however high the volume is set."
    state_key: speaker_level_limit
    default: 100
    min: 0
    max: 100
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker
      body: '{"levelLimiter": {value}}'
  sound_profile:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Wallmount", label: "Wall mount" }
      - { value: "TableTop", label: "Table top" }
      - { value: "AboveDisplay", label: "Above display" }
      - { value: "UnderDisplay", label: "Under display" }
      - { value: "FreeStanding", label: "Free standing" }
      - { value: "Custom", label: "Custom (uses the microphone EQ)" }
    label: Sound Profile
    help: "Tunes the microphone for how the bar is mounted. Custom uses the seven-band microphone EQ instead."
    state_key: sound_profile
    default: "Wallmount"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/soundProfile
      body: '{"preset": "{value}"}'
  noise_gate_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Noise Gate
    help: "Keeps background noise out between sentences."
    state_key: noise_gate_enabled
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate
      body: '{"enabled": {value}}'
  noise_gate_threshold_db:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Threshold
    help: "-70 to -30 dB: the level below which the gate closes."
    state_key: noise_gate_threshold_db
    default: -40
    min: -70
    max: -30
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate
      body: '{"threshold": {value}}'
  noise_gate_hold_ms:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Hold Time
    help: "100 to 500 ms the gate stays open after the level drops."
    state_key: noise_gate_hold_ms
    default: 300
    min: 100
    max: 500
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate
      body: '{"holdTime": {value}}'
  noise_gate_range_db:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Range
    help: "-80 to 0 dB: how far the gate turns the microphone down when it closes."
    state_key: noise_gate_range_db
    default: -40
    min: -80
    max: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate
      body: '{"range": {value}}'
  noise_suppression:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Low", label: "Low" }
      - { value: "Medium", label: "Medium" }
      - { value: "High", label: "High" }
    label: Noise Suppression
    help: "How hard the bar filters steady background noise out of the microphones."
    state_key: noise_suppression
    default: "Medium"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/noiseSuppression
      body: '{"weighting": "{value}"}'
  mixer_fade:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Slow", label: "Slow" }
      - { value: "Medium", label: "Medium" }
      - { value: "Fast", label: "Fast" }
    label: Mic Selector Fade
    help: "How quickly the mixer fades between the bar's microphone and the Dante extension microphones."
    state_key: mixer_fade
    default: "Medium"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/mixer
      body: '{"fadeBehavior": "{value}"}'
  conference_out_far_end_db:
    type: integer
    label: Conference Output Far End Gain
    help: "-60 to 0 dB of the far end in the Dante conference output (the mix for an assistive listening system). Mind clipping: it adds to the near end."
    state_key: conference_out_far_end_db
    default: -6
    min: -60
    max: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput
      body: '{"farEndGain": {value}}'
  conference_out_near_end_db:
    type: integer
    label: Conference Output Near End Gain
    help: "-60 to 0 dB of the bar's microphones in the Dante conference output. Mind clipping: it adds to the far end."
    state_key: conference_out_near_end_db
    default: -6
    min: -60
    max: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput
      body: '{"nearEndGain": {value}}'
  dante_input_1_gain_db:
    type: integer
    label: Dante Input 1 Gain
    help: "-60 to 0 dB for the extension microphone on Dante input 1, as the mic selector hears it."
    state_key: dante_input_1_gain_db
    default: 0
    min: -60
    max: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/dante/0
      body: '{"gain": {value}}'
  dante_input_2_gain_db:
    type: integer
    label: Dante Input 2 Gain
    help: "-60 to 0 dB for the extension microphone on Dante input 2, as the mic selector hears it."
    state_key: dante_input_2_gain_db
    default: 0
    min: -60
    max: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/dante/1
      body: '{"gain": {value}}'
  dante_continuous_stream:
    type: boolean
    label: Continuous Dante Stream
    help: "Keeps the Dante outputs playing when no computer is connected over USB; otherwise they are muted."
    state_key: dante_continuous_stream
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/interfaces/network/dante/settings
      body: '{"continuousDanteStream": {value}}'
  dante_speaker_output:
    type: boolean
    label: Dante Speaker Output
    help: "Sends the far end to external Dante speakers and turns the bar's own speakers off."
    state_key: dante_speaker_output
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/interfaces/network/dante/settings
      body: '{"danteSpeakerOutput": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 1
    help: "The beam ignores sound from inside the zone (a projector fan, a doorway)."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_enabled
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0
      body: '{"enabled": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_left:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Left Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_left
    default: 15
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0
      body: '{"left": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_right:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Right Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_right
    default: 30
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0
      body: '{"right": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 2
    help: "The beam ignores sound from inside the zone (a projector fan, a doorway)."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_enabled
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1
      body: '{"enabled": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_left:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Left Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_left
    default: 15
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1
      body: '{"left": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_right:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Right Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_right
    default: 30
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1
      body: '{"right": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 3
    help: "The beam ignores sound from inside the zone (a projector fan, a doorway)."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_enabled
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2
      body: '{"enabled": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_left:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Left Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_left
    default: 15
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2
      body: '{"left": {value}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_right:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Right Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_right
    default: 30
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2
      body: '{"right": {value}}'
  priority_zone_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Priority Zone
    help: "Gives a talker inside the zone (a presenter's spot) priority in the mixer."
    state_key: priority_zone_enabled
    default: false
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0
      body: '{"enabled": {value}}'
  priority_zone_gain:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Low", label: "Low" }
      - { value: "Medium", label: "Medium" }
      - { value: "High", label: "High" }
    label: Priority Zone Gain
    help: "How strongly a talker in the priority zone is favoured."
    state_key: priority_zone_gain
    default: "Medium"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0
      body: '{"gain": "{value}"}'
  priority_zone_left:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Left Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: priority_zone_left
    default: 15
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0
      body: '{"left": {value}}'
  priority_zone_right:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Right Edge
    help: "15 to 165 degrees across the bar's pickup area."
    state_key: priority_zone_right
    default: 30
    min: 15
    max: 165
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0
      body: '{"right": {value}}'
  camera_zoom_speed:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Slow", label: "Slow" }
      - { value: "Medium", label: "Medium" }
      - { value: "Fast", label: "Fast" }
    label: Remote Zoom Speed
    help: "How fast the remote control's zoom buttons zoom."
    state_key: camera_zoom_speed
    default: "Medium"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement
      body: '{"zoomSpeed": "{value}"}'
  camera_pan_tilt_speed:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Slow", label: "Slow" }
      - { value: "Medium", label: "Medium" }
      - { value: "Fast", label: "Fast" }
    label: Remote Pan and Tilt Speed
    help: "How fast the remote control's arrow buttons move the camera."
    state_key: camera_pan_tilt_speed
    default: "Medium"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement
      body: '{"panTiltSpeed": "{value}"}'
  autoframing_speed:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "Slow", label: "Slow" }
      - { value: "Medium", label: "Medium" }
      - { value: "Fast", label: "Fast" }
    label: Auto Framing Speed
    help: "How quickly auto framing follows the people in view."
    state_key: autoframing_speed
    default: "Medium"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement
      body: '{"autoFramingSpeed": "{value}"}'
  autoframing_button_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Remote Auto Framing Button
    help: "Whether the remote control's auto framing button works."
    state_key: autoframing_button_enabled
    default: true
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess
      body: '{"autoFramingAccessEnabled": {value}}'
  person_tiling_button_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Remote Person Tiling Button
    help: "Whether the remote control's person tiling button works."
    state_key: person_tiling_button_enabled
    default: true
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess
      body: '{"personTilingAccessEnabled": {value}}'
  led_brightness:
    type: integer
    label: LED Brightness
    help: "0 (off) to 5."
    state_key: led_brightness
    default: 3
    min: 0
    max: 5
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/device/leds/ring
      body: '{"brightness": {value}}'
  sound_prompts:
    type: boolean
    label: Sound Prompts
    help: "The bar's own sound feedback. The welcome sound plays at every boot regardless."
    state_key: sound_prompts
    default: true
    setup: false
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/device/feedback
      body: '{"soundPrompts": {value}}'
  standby_mode:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "EcoMode", label: "Eco (network standby, wakes remotely)" }
      - { value: "LowPowerMode", label: "Low power (deep sleep, wakes by hand)" }
      - { value: "AlwaysOn", label: "Always on" }
    label: Standby Mode
    help: >
      The lowest energy-saving state the bar may enter. Eco keeps it
      reachable on the network. Low power lets it sleep only once nothing is
      connected, Ethernet included, for up to 2.5 hours, and then it wakes
      only from its own power button. Always on never saves energy.
    state_key: standby_mode
    default: "EcoMode"
    setup: false
    write:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/device/allowedStandbyMode
      body: '{"mode": "{value}"}'

commands:
  # ── Queries (polled; the session covers everything else) ──
  query_identity:
    label: Query Identity
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/identity
    query_for: product
    help: "Reads the product code (Bar S or Bar M), article number, serial and hardware revision"
  query_ssc_version:
    label: Query API Version
    method: GET
    path: /api/ssc/version
    query_for: ssc_schema_version
    help: "Reads the SSC protocol and API schema versions the bar runs"
  query_site:
    label: Query Device Name
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/site
    query_for: device_name
    help: "Reads the bar's device name, Dante name, location and position"
  query_state:
    label: Query Device State
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/state
    query_for: device_state
    help: "Reads the bar's state and its warnings"
  query_firmware:
    label: Query Firmware
    method: GET
    path: /api/firmware/update/state
    query_for: firmware_version
    help: "Reads the firmware version and the state of any update"
  query_identification:
    label: Query Identify
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/identification
    query_for: identify_active
    help: "Reads whether the bar is flashing to identify itself"
  query_speaker:
    label: Query Volume
    method: GET
    path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker
    query_for: volume
    help: "Reads the speaker volume and its limit"
  query_user_interaction:
    label: Query User Interaction
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/hasUserInteraction
    query_for: user_interaction
    help: "Reads whether the bar reports someone using it"

  # ── Device ──
  identify_on:
    label: Identify Bar
    method: PUT
    path: /api/device/identification
    body: '{"visual": true}'
    help: "Flashes the bar's LEDs so you can see which one this is"
    sets: { identify_active: true }
  identify_off:
    label: Stop Identifying Bar
    method: PUT
    path: /api/device/identification
    body: '{"visual": false}'
    help: "Stops the identify flashing"
    sets: { identify_active: false }
  restart:
    label: Restart Bar
    method: PUT
    path: /api/device/restart
    help: "Restarts the bar. The camera, microphones and speakers drop out until it is back."
    # Not measured: no TC Bar on the bench and no Sennheiser document gives a
    # boot time. 120 s is a ceiling to be replaced by the measured time
    # rounded up (the hardware checklist in the shipped record).
    restarts_device_for: 120
  set_device_profile:
    label: Set Device Profile
    method: PUT
    path: /api/device/profile
    body: '{"configuration": "{profile}"}'
    help: "Switches the bar to its own Custom settings or to the Zoom or Microsoft Teams profile. Resets every camera setting and restarts the bar; Microsoft Teams also turns the HDMI output off."
    confirm: "Resets every camera setting and restarts the bar."
    # Same unmeasured window as restart: the profile change reboots the bar.
    restarts_device_for: 120
    params:
      profile:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Profile
        values:
          - { value: "Custom", label: "Custom" }
          - { value: "Zoom", label: "Zoom" }
          - { value: "MicrosoftTeams", label: "Microsoft Teams" }
    sets: { device_profile: "{profile}" }

  # ── Audio ──
  mute_on:
    label: Mute Microphones
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/mute
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "Mutes the bar's microphone and any Dante extension microphones"
    sets: { mute: true }
  mute_off:
    label: Unmute Microphones
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/mute
    body: '{"enabled": false}'
    help: "Unmutes the bar's microphones"
    sets: { mute: false }
  set_volume:
    label: Set Volume
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker
    body: '{"volume": {level}}'
    help: "Sets the bar's speaker volume, 0 to 100%"
    params:
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Volume
        min: 0
        max: 100
        unit: "%"
    sets: { volume: "{level}" }
  volume_up:
    label: Volume Up
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker/relative
    body: '{"volumeUp": {steps}}'
    help: "Turns the speaker volume up by the given steps; it stops at the top"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 5
  volume_down:
    label: Volume Down
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker/relative
    body: '{"volumeDown": {steps}}'
    help: "Turns the speaker volume down by the given steps; it stops at 0"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 5
  set_mic_eq:
    label: Set Microphone EQ
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq
    body: '[{band1}, {band2}, {band3}, {band4}, {band5}, {band6}, {band7}]'
    help: "Sets all seven bands of the microphone's custom EQ, -8 to +8 dB each, lowest band first. The Custom sound profile uses it."
    params:
      band1:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 1 (lowest)
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band2:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 2
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band3:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 3
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band4:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 4
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band5:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 5
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band6:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 6
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band7:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 7 (highest)
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
    sets: { mic_eq_1: "{band1}", mic_eq_2: "{band2}", mic_eq_3: "{band3}", mic_eq_4: "{band4}", mic_eq_5: "{band5}", mic_eq_6: "{band6}", mic_eq_7: "{band7}" }
  mic_eq_flat:
    label: Flatten Microphone EQ
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq
    body: '[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]'
    help: "Sets every band of the microphone's custom EQ to 0 dB"
    sets: { mic_eq_1: 0, mic_eq_2: 0, mic_eq_3: 0, mic_eq_4: 0, mic_eq_5: 0, mic_eq_6: 0, mic_eq_7: 0 }
  set_speaker_eq:
    label: Set Speaker EQ
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq
    body: '[{band1}, {band2}, {band3}, {band4}, {band5}, {band6}, {band7}]'
    help: "Sets all seven bands of the speaker's custom EQ, -8 to +8 dB each, lowest band first"
    params:
      band1:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 1 (lowest)
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band2:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 2
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band3:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 3
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band4:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 4
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band5:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 5
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band6:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 6
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
      band7:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Band 7 (highest)
        min: -8
        max: 8
        unit: dB
    sets: { speaker_eq_1: "{band1}", speaker_eq_2: "{band2}", speaker_eq_3: "{band3}", speaker_eq_4: "{band4}", speaker_eq_5: "{band5}", speaker_eq_6: "{band6}", speaker_eq_7: "{band7}" }
  speaker_eq_flat:
    label: Flatten Speaker EQ
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq
    body: '[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]'
    help: "Sets every band of the speaker's custom EQ to 0 dB"
    sets: { speaker_eq_1: 0, speaker_eq_2: 0, speaker_eq_3: 0, speaker_eq_4: 0, speaker_eq_5: 0, speaker_eq_6: 0, speaker_eq_7: 0 }
  exclusion_zone_on:
    label: Exclusion Zone On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/{zone}
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "Turns an exclusion zone on: the beam ignores sound from inside it"
    params:
      zone:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Zone
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Zone 1" }
          - { value: "2", label: "Zone 2" }
          - { value: "3", label: "Zone 3" }
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2 }
  exclusion_zone_off:
    label: Exclusion Zone Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/{zone}
    body: '{"enabled": false}'
    help: "Turns an exclusion zone off"
    params:
      zone:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Zone
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Zone 1" }
          - { value: "2", label: "Zone 2" }
          - { value: "3", label: "Zone 3" }
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2 }
  priority_zone_on:
    label: Priority Zone On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "Turns the priority zone on: a talker inside it is favoured in the mixer"
    sets: { priority_zone_enabled: true }
  priority_zone_off:
    label: Priority Zone Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0
    body: '{"enabled": false}'
    help: "Turns the priority zone off"
    sets: { priority_zone_enabled: false }

  # ── Camera ──
  autoframing_on:
    label: Auto Framing On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess
    body: '{"autoFramingEnabled": true}'
    help: "The camera frames the people in view by itself"
    sets: { autoframing: true }
  autoframing_off:
    label: Auto Framing Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess
    body: '{"autoFramingEnabled": false}'
    help: "Stops auto framing; the camera holds its view"
    sets: { autoframing: false }
  person_tiling_on:
    label: Person Tiling On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess
    body: '{"personTilingEnabled": true}'
    help: "Shows each person in view in a tile of their own"
    sets: { person_tiling: true }
  person_tiling_off:
    label: Person Tiling Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess
    body: '{"personTilingEnabled": false}'
    help: "Stops person tiling"
    sets: { person_tiling: false }
  camera_full_view:
    label: Camera Full View
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/ffov
    help: "Returns the camera to its full field of view"
    sets: { camera_pan: 0, camera_tilt: 0, camera_zoom: 100 }
  camera_preset_recall:
    label: Recall Camera Preset
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/preset/load
    help: "Moves the camera to its stored preset view"
  camera_preset_save:
    label: Save Camera Preset
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/preset/store
    help: "Stores the camera's current view as its preset, replacing the one stored"
  set_camera_pan:
    label: Set Camera Pan
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement
    body: '{"panPosition": {pan}}'
    help: "Pans the camera to a position from -25 to 25"
    params:
      pan:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Pan
        min: -25
        max: 25
    sets: { camera_pan: "{pan}" }
  set_camera_tilt:
    label: Set Camera Tilt
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement
    body: '{"tiltPosition": {tilt}}'
    help: "Tilts the camera to a position from -25 to 25"
    params:
      tilt:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Tilt
        min: -25
        max: 25
    sets: { camera_tilt: "{tilt}" }
  set_camera_zoom:
    label: Set Camera Zoom
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement
    body: '{"zoomPosition": {zoom}}'
    help: "Zooms the camera: 100 is no zoom. Bar M up to 500 (150 in the Microsoft Teams profile); Bar S up to 300 (400 in the Zoom profile, 200 in Microsoft Teams)"
    params:
      zoom:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Zoom
        min: 100
        max: 500
    sets: { camera_zoom: "{zoom}" }
  camera_left:
    label: Camera Left
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative
    body: '{"left": {steps}}'
    help: "Pans the camera left by the given steps; it stops at the end of its travel"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 1
  camera_right:
    label: Camera Right
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative
    body: '{"right": {steps}}'
    help: "Pans the camera right by the given steps; it stops at the end of its travel"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 1
  camera_up:
    label: Camera Up
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative
    body: '{"up": {steps}}'
    help: "Tilts the camera up by the given steps; it stops at the end of its travel"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 1
  camera_down:
    label: Camera Down
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative
    body: '{"down": {steps}}'
    help: "Tilts the camera down by the given steps; it stops at the end of its travel"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 1
  camera_zoom_in:
    label: Camera Zoom In
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative
    body: '{"zoomIn": {steps}}'
    help: "Zooms the camera in by the given steps (zoom runs 100 to 500); it stops at the model's limit"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 10
  camera_zoom_out:
    label: Camera Zoom Out
    method: PUT
    path: /api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative
    body: '{"zoomOut": {steps}}'
    help: "Zooms the camera out by the given steps; it stops at no zoom"
    params:
      steps:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Steps
        min: 1
        max: 255
        default: 10

  # ── Bluetooth ──
  bluetooth_on:
    label: Bluetooth On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/interfaces/bluetooth
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "Turns the bar's Bluetooth on. Wait ten seconds before starting pairing."
    sets: { bluetooth_enabled: true }
  bluetooth_off:
    label: Bluetooth Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/interfaces/bluetooth
    body: '{"enabled": false}'
    help: "Turns Bluetooth off, which also stops pairing and forgets the paired devices"
    sets: { bluetooth_enabled: false, bluetooth_pairing: false }
  bluetooth_pairing_on:
    label: Start Bluetooth Pairing
    method: PUT
    path: /api/interfaces/bluetooth
    body: '{"pairing": true}'
    help: "Makes the bar visible for pairing for three minutes or until a phone connects. Bluetooth must have been on for ten seconds."
    sets: { bluetooth_pairing: true }
  bluetooth_pairing_off:
    label: Stop Bluetooth Pairing
    method: PUT
    path: /api/interfaces/bluetooth
    body: '{"pairing": false}'
    help: "Stops pairing"
    sets: { bluetooth_pairing: false }

  # ── Feeds (at runtime) ──
  talker_position_on:
    label: Talker Position On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/beam", "/api/audio/inputs/mixer/activity"]'
    help: "Starts streaming the beam angle and which microphone the mixer picked"
  talker_position_off:
    label: Talker Position Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/remove
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/beam", "/api/audio/inputs/mixer/activity"]'
    help: "Stops the talker position feed"
  meters_on:
    label: Meters On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/maxLevel", "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/level", "/api/audio/inputs/usb", "/api/audio/inputs/bluetooth", "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0/level", "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1/level"]'
    help: "Starts streaming the microphone, USB, Bluetooth and Dante input levels"
  meters_off:
    label: Meters Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/remove
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/maxLevel", "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/level", "/api/audio/inputs/usb", "/api/audio/inputs/bluetooth", "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0/level", "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1/level"]'
    help: "Stops the level meter feed"

  # ── Subscription session (run by the push block; here so they are visible) ──
  subscribe_device:
    label: "Subscribe: device state"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/device/state", "/api/device/site", "/api/device/identification", "/api/firmware/update/state"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_audio:
    label: "Subscribe: mute and volume"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/mute", "/api/audio/outputs/speaker", "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_audio_processing:
    label: "Subscribe: audio processing"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate", "/api/audio/inputs/noiseSuppression", "/api/audio/soundProfile", "/api/audio/inputs/mixer", "/api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_equalizers:
    label: "Subscribe: equalizers"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq", "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_zones:
    label: "Subscribe: beam zones"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0", "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1", "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2", "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_dante_inputs:
    label: "Subscribe: Dante inputs"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/audio/inputs/dante/0", "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_camera:
    label: "Subscribe: camera"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess", "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement", "/api/video/input/internalCamera", "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters", "/api/video/output/hdmi"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_device_settings:
    label: "Subscribe: device settings"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/device/hasUserInteraction", "/api/device/profile", "/api/device/allowedStandbyMode", "/api/device/leds/ring", "/api/device/feedback"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_network:
    label: "Subscribe: network"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/interfaces/network/portConfiguration", "/api/interfaces/network/wifi", "/api/interfaces/bluetooth", "/api/interfaces/network/dante", "/api/interfaces/network/dante/settings"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  subscribe_poe_output:
    label: "Subscribe: PoE output"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/device/power/poe/output"]'
    help: "Sent automatically each time the event stream opens; there is no need to send it by hand"
  end_subscription:
    label: "Subscribe: end session"
    method: DELETE
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}
    help: "Sent automatically when the device is disconnected on purpose"

# ── Responses ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every body is JSON, so every rule is json: true and all of them run
# against every body. Two shapes arrive:
#   - a polled GET answers with the bare resource ({"volume": ..}). Only
#     the resources whose bodies carry a key no other resource has are
#     polled, and those rules are scoped with require: to it;
#   - the subscription stream sends {"<resource path>": {..}} (SSCv2 spec,
#     "Subscription notification syntax"), possibly several resources in
#     one object, so those rules read the path as the leading JSON key. A
#     path only ever appears in stream bodies, so they need no require:.
responses:
  # ── Polled bodies ──
  # /api/device/identity
  - json: true
    require: product
    set:
      product: "product"
      model: { key: "product", map: { "TCBarS": "TeamConnect Bar S", "TCBarM": "TeamConnect Bar M" } }
      article_number: "articleNumber"
      serial: "serial"
      hardware_revision: "hardwareRevision"
      vendor: "vendor"
  # /api/ssc/version
  - json: true
    require: schema
    set:
      ssc_protocol_version: "protocol"
      ssc_schema_version: "schema"
  # /api/device/site
  - json: true
    require: deviceName
    set:
      device_name: "deviceName"
      dante_name: "danteName"
      location: "location"
      position: "position"
  # /api/device/state: the warnings array becomes one boolean per flag
  - json: true
    require: warnings
    set:
      device_state: "state"
      warning_count: "warnings"
      warning_mic_muted: { key: "warnings", contains: "MicMuted" }
      warning_lens_cap_on: { key: "warnings", contains: "LensCapOn" }
      warning_camera_off: { key: "warnings", contains: "CameraOff" }
      warning_speaker_muted: { key: "warnings", contains: "SpeakerMuted" }
      warning_no_device_connected: { key: "warnings", contains: "NoDeviceConnected" }
      warning_overheating: { key: "warnings", contains: "DeviceOverheating" }
      warning_cpu_overloaded: { key: "warnings", contains: "CpuOverloading" }
      warning_bluetooth_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "BluetoothFailure" }
      warning_dante_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "DanteFailure" }
      warning_mic_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "MicFailure" }
      warning_speaker_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "SpeakerFailure" }
      warning_voice_engine_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "VoiceEngineFailure" }
      warning_camera_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "CameraFailure" }
      warning_usb_failure: { key: "warnings", contains: "UsbFailure" }
      warning_time_uninitialized: { key: "warnings", contains: "TimeUninitialized" }
      warning_network_loop: { key: "warnings", contains: "NetworkLoopDetected" }
  # /api/firmware/update/state
  - json: true
    require: deviceVersion
    set:
      firmware_version: "deviceVersion"
      update_state: "state"
      update_progress: "progress"
      update_last_status: "lastStatus"
  # /api/device/identification
  - json: true
    require: visual
    set:
      identify_active: "visual"
  # /api/audio/outputs/speaker
  - json: true
    require: [volume, levelLimiter]
    set:
      volume: "volume"
      speaker_level_limit: "levelLimiter"
  # /api/device/hasUserInteraction
  - json: true
    require: interaction
    set:
      user_interaction: "interaction"

  # ── Stream bodies: device ──
  - json: true
    set:
      device_state: "/api/device/state.state"
      warning_count: "/api/device/state.warnings"
      warning_mic_muted: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "MicMuted" }
      warning_lens_cap_on: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "LensCapOn" }
      warning_camera_off: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "CameraOff" }
      warning_speaker_muted: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "SpeakerMuted" }
      warning_no_device_connected: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "NoDeviceConnected" }
      warning_overheating: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "DeviceOverheating" }
      warning_cpu_overloaded: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "CpuOverloading" }
      warning_bluetooth_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "BluetoothFailure" }
      warning_dante_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "DanteFailure" }
      warning_mic_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "MicFailure" }
      warning_speaker_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "SpeakerFailure" }
      warning_voice_engine_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "VoiceEngineFailure" }
      warning_camera_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "CameraFailure" }
      warning_usb_failure: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "UsbFailure" }
      warning_time_uninitialized: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "TimeUninitialized" }
      warning_network_loop: { key: "/api/device/state.warnings", contains: "NetworkLoopDetected" }
  - json: true
    set:
      device_name: "/api/device/site.deviceName"
      dante_name: "/api/device/site.danteName"
      location: "/api/device/site.location"
      position: "/api/device/site.position"
  - json: true
    set:
      identify_active: "/api/device/identification.visual"
  - json: true
    set:
      firmware_version: "/api/firmware/update/state.deviceVersion"
      update_state: "/api/firmware/update/state.state"
      update_progress: "/api/firmware/update/state.progress"
      update_last_status: "/api/firmware/update/state.lastStatus"
  - json: true
    set:
      user_interaction: "/api/device/hasUserInteraction.interaction"
  - json: true
    set:
      device_profile: "/api/device/profile.configuration"
  - json: true
    set:
      standby_mode: "/api/device/allowedStandbyMode.mode"
  - json: true
    set:
      led_brightness: "/api/device/leds/ring.brightness"
  - json: true
    set:
      sound_prompts: "/api/device/feedback.soundPrompts"
  - json: true
    set:
      poe_output_enabled: "/api/device/power/poe/output.enabled"

  # ── Stream bodies: network ──
  - json: true
    set:
      port_configuration: "/api/interfaces/network/portConfiguration.configuration"
  - json: true
    set:
      wifi_enabled: "/api/interfaces/network/wifi.enabled"
      wifi_connected: { key: "/api/interfaces/network/wifi.state", type: boolean, map: { "Connected": true, "Disconnected": false } }
      wifi_ssid: "/api/interfaces/network/wifi.connection.ssid"
      wifi_signal: "/api/interfaces/network/wifi.connection.signal"
      wifi_band: "/api/interfaces/network/wifi.connection.frequency"
  - json: true
    set:
      bluetooth_enabled: "/api/interfaces/bluetooth.enabled"
      bluetooth_pairing: "/api/interfaces/bluetooth.pairing"
      bluetooth_mac: "/api/interfaces/bluetooth.mac"
  - json: true
    set:
      dante_enabled: "/api/interfaces/network/dante.enabled"
  - json: true
    set:
      dante_continuous_stream: "/api/interfaces/network/dante/settings.continuousDanteStream"
      dante_speaker_output: "/api/interfaces/network/dante/settings.danteSpeakerOutput"

  # ── Stream bodies: audio ──
  - json: true
    set:
      mute: "/api/audio/inputs/mute.enabled"
  - json: true
    set:
      volume: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker.volume"
      speaker_level_limit: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker.levelLimiter"
  - json: true
    set:
      mic_enabled: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic.enabled"
      mic_gain_db: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic.gain"
  - json: true
    set:
      noise_gate_enabled: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate.enabled"
      noise_gate_threshold_db: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate.threshold"
      noise_gate_hold_ms: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate.holdTime"
      noise_gate_range_db: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate.range"
  - json: true
    set:
      noise_suppression: "/api/audio/inputs/noiseSuppression.weighting"
  - json: true
    set:
      sound_profile: "/api/audio/soundProfile.preset"
  - json: true
    set:
      mixer_fade: "/api/audio/inputs/mixer.fadeBehavior"
  - json: true
    set:
      conference_out_far_end_db: "/api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput.farEndGain"
      conference_out_near_end_db: "/api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput.nearEndGain"
  - json: true
    set:
      dante_input_1_gain_db: "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0.gain"
  - json: true
    set:
      dante_input_2_gain_db: "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1.gain"
  - json: true
    set:
      mic_eq_1: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.0"
      mic_eq_2: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.1"
      mic_eq_3: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.2"
      mic_eq_4: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.3"
      mic_eq_5: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.4"
      mic_eq_6: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.5"
      mic_eq_7: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq.6"
  - json: true
    set:
      speaker_eq_1: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.0"
      speaker_eq_2: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.1"
      speaker_eq_3: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.2"
      speaker_eq_4: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.3"
      speaker_eq_5: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.4"
      speaker_eq_6: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.5"
      speaker_eq_7: "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq.6"
  - json: true
    set:
      exclusion_zone_1_enabled: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0.enabled"
      exclusion_zone_1_active: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0.active"
      exclusion_zone_1_left: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0.left"
      exclusion_zone_1_right: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0.right"
  - json: true
    set:
      exclusion_zone_2_enabled: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1.enabled"
      exclusion_zone_2_active: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1.active"
      exclusion_zone_2_left: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1.left"
      exclusion_zone_2_right: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1.right"
  - json: true
    set:
      exclusion_zone_3_enabled: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2.enabled"
      exclusion_zone_3_active: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2.active"
      exclusion_zone_3_left: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2.left"
      exclusion_zone_3_right: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2.right"
  - json: true
    set:
      priority_zone_enabled: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0.enabled"
      priority_zone_active: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0.active"
      priority_zone_gain: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0.gain"
      priority_zone_left: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0.left"
      priority_zone_right: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0.right"

  # ── Stream bodies: talker position feed ──
  # Throttled like the meters. The beam reports a new angle as the talker
  # moves; the throttle writes the newest angle when each window ends, so
  # the angle the talker stopped at is the one a camera macro reads.
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      beam_azimuth: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/beam.position"
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      active_mic: "/api/audio/inputs/mixer/activity.activeChannel"

  # ── Stream bodies: level meters ──
  # One rule per meter: the throttle window is per rule, so a shared rule
  # would let one meter starve the rest.
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      max_peak_db: "/api/audio/inputs/maxLevel.peak"
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      mic_peak_db: "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/level.peak"
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      usb_level_db: "/api/audio/inputs/usb.level"
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      bluetooth_level_db: "/api/audio/inputs/bluetooth.level"
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      dante_input_1_level_db: "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0/level.value"
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      dante_input_2_level_db: "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1/level.value"

  # ── Stream bodies: camera ──
  - json: true
    set:
      autoframing: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess.autoFramingEnabled"
      person_tiling: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess.personTilingEnabled"
      autoframing_button_enabled: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess.autoFramingAccessEnabled"
      person_tiling_button_enabled: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess.personTilingAccessEnabled"
  - json: true
    set:
      camera_pan: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement.panPosition"
      camera_tilt: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement.tiltPosition"
      camera_zoom: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement.zoomPosition"
      camera_zoom_speed: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement.zoomSpeed"
      camera_pan_tilt_speed: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement.panTiltSpeed"
      autoframing_speed: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement.autoFramingSpeed"
  - json: true
    set:
      camera_active: "/api/video/input/internalCamera.active"
  - json: true
    set:
      camera_compensation: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.compensation"
      camera_anti_flicker: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.antiFlickerFrequency"
      camera_brightness: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.brightness"
      camera_contrast: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.contrast"
      camera_saturation: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.saturation"
      camera_sharpness: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.sharpness"
      camera_auto_white_balance: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.autoWhitebalanceEnabled"
      camera_white_balance_k: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.whitebalance"
      camera_default_mode: "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters.defaultCameraMode"
  - json: true
    set:
      hdmi_enabled: "/api/video/output/hdmi.enabled"

on_connect:
  - query_identity
  - query_ssc_version
  - query_site
  - query_state
  - query_firmware
  - query_identification
  - query_speaker
  - query_user_interaction

# The resources whose bodies can be told apart without their path; the
# session resends everything else on every reopen.
polling:
  queries:
    - query_state
    - query_speaker
    - query_user_interaction
    - query_identification
    - query_firmware
    - query_site

# ── Simulator ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One dispatcher handler plays the bar: it parses the synthesized request
# line, answers GETs from state, applies PUTs to state and, like the real
# bar, sends the changed resource on the subscription stream afterwards.
# The subscription requests record what the driver asked for and answer
# with the current value of every newly subscribed resource, which is what
# makes the driver's state complete after a (re)open. The push block's
# session header and opening event come from the platform.
#
# The model is the "product" state value (TCBarM or TCBarS, a selector in
# the Simulator UI): it decides the camera's zoom ceiling and whether the
# Split network mode exists. "hidden_paths" (comma-separated resource paths,
# set from a script) plays an older firmware: a subscription list naming one
# of them is refused whole, as the SSCv2 spec requires.
#
# Fidelity gaps, on purpose: the simulator answers only 200 or 404, so a
# refusal the bar answers 400, 409 or 422 (a zoom past the model's ceiling,
# a wrong session id, an identify conflict) is a 404 or, where it can be
# applied, a clamped value. Any session id is accepted and Basic auth is not
# checked. Restart and a device profile change answer and stay up (the bar
# closes the stream and reboots). Changes made from the Simulator UI are
# sent whether or not their resource is subscribed, and a warning toggled
# there is sent as the only flag in the warnings array.
simulator:
  initial_state:
    product: "TCBarM"
    model: "TeamConnect Bar M"
    article_number: "700111"
    serial: "1023456789"
    hardware_revision: "MP"
    vendor: "Sennheiser electronic SE & Co. KG"
    device_name: "TCBarM-c8ec48"
    dante_name: "TCBarM-c8ec49"
    location: "Building 5, Room 15"
    position: "Above the display"
    ssc_protocol_version: "2.3"
    ssc_schema_version: "1.16"
    device_state: "Normal"
    warning_count: 0
    warning_mic_muted: false
    warning_lens_cap_on: false
    warning_camera_off: false
    warning_speaker_muted: false
    warning_no_device_connected: false
    warning_overheating: false
    warning_cpu_overloaded: false
    warning_bluetooth_failure: false
    warning_dante_failure: false
    warning_mic_failure: false
    warning_speaker_failure: false
    warning_voice_engine_failure: false
    warning_camera_failure: false
    warning_usb_failure: false
    warning_time_uninitialized: false
    warning_network_loop: false
    identify_active: false
    user_interaction: false
    device_profile: "Custom"
    firmware_version: "1.16.0"
    update_state: "Idle"
    update_progress: 0
    update_last_status: "None"
    standby_mode: "EcoMode"
    led_brightness: 3
    sound_prompts: true
    poe_output_enabled: false
    port_configuration: "Split"
    wifi_enabled: false
    wifi_connected: false
    wifi_ssid: ""
    wifi_signal: 0
    wifi_band: ""
    bluetooth_enabled: false
    bluetooth_pairing: false
    bluetooth_mac: "00:1b:66:c8:ec:53"
    dante_enabled: true
    dante_continuous_stream: false
    dante_speaker_output: false
    mute: false
    volume: 50
    speaker_level_limit: 100
    mic_enabled: true
    mic_gain_db: 0
    noise_gate_enabled: false
    noise_gate_threshold_db: -40
    noise_gate_hold_ms: 300
    noise_gate_range_db: -40
    noise_suppression: "Medium"
    sound_profile: "Wallmount"
    mixer_fade: "Medium"
    conference_out_far_end_db: -6
    conference_out_near_end_db: -6
    dante_input_1_gain_db: 0
    dante_input_2_gain_db: 0
    mic_eq_1: 0
    mic_eq_2: 0
    mic_eq_3: 0
    mic_eq_4: 0
    mic_eq_5: 0
    mic_eq_6: 0
    mic_eq_7: 0
    speaker_eq_1: 0
    speaker_eq_2: 0
    speaker_eq_3: 0
    speaker_eq_4: 0
    speaker_eq_5: 0
    speaker_eq_6: 0
    speaker_eq_7: 0
    exclusion_zone_1_enabled: false
    exclusion_zone_1_active: false
    exclusion_zone_1_left: 15
    exclusion_zone_1_right: 30
    exclusion_zone_2_enabled: false
    exclusion_zone_2_active: false
    exclusion_zone_2_left: 75
    exclusion_zone_2_right: 90
    exclusion_zone_3_enabled: false
    exclusion_zone_3_active: false
    exclusion_zone_3_left: 150
    exclusion_zone_3_right: 165
    priority_zone_enabled: false
    priority_zone_active: false
    priority_zone_gain: "Medium"
    priority_zone_left: 80
    priority_zone_right: 100
    beam_azimuth: 90
    active_mic: "InternalMic"
    max_peak_db: -40
    mic_peak_db: -40
    usb_level_db: -60
    bluetooth_level_db: -60
    dante_input_1_level_db: -60
    dante_input_2_level_db: -60
    camera_active: false
    autoframing: true
    person_tiling: false
    autoframing_button_enabled: true
    person_tiling_button_enabled: true
    camera_pan: 0
    camera_tilt: 0
    camera_zoom: 100
    camera_zoom_speed: "Medium"
    camera_pan_tilt_speed: "Medium"
    autoframing_speed: "Medium"
    hdmi_enabled: true
    camera_compensation: "Backlight"
    camera_anti_flicker: "Auto"
    camera_brightness: 0
    camera_contrast: 5
    camera_saturation: 5
    camera_sharpness: 2
    camera_auto_white_balance: true
    camera_white_balance_k: 4600
    camera_default_mode: "ResumeLastView"
    # Simulator bookkeeping, not driver state
    subscribed_paths: ""
    hidden_paths: ""
    preset_pan: 0
    preset_tilt: 0
    preset_zoom: 100

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02

  # Changes made from the Simulator UI reach the stream through these; a
  # PUT from the driver is answered by the dispatcher below, which sends the
  # whole resource.
  notifications:
    device_state: '{"/api/device/state": {"state": "{value}"}}'
    mute:
      "true": '{"/api/audio/inputs/mute": {"enabled": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/audio/inputs/mute": {"enabled": false}}'
    volume: '{"/api/audio/outputs/speaker": {"volume": {value}}}'
    identify_active:
      "true": '{"/api/device/identification": {"visual": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/device/identification": {"visual": false}}'
    user_interaction:
      "true": '{"/api/device/hasUserInteraction": {"interaction": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/device/hasUserInteraction": {"interaction": false}}'
    camera_active:
      "true": '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera": {"active": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera": {"active": false}}'
    autoframing:
      "true": '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess": {"autoFramingEnabled": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess": {"autoFramingEnabled": false}}'
    person_tiling:
      "true": '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess": {"personTilingEnabled": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess": {"personTilingEnabled": false}}'
    camera_zoom: '{"/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement": {"zoomPosition": {value}}}'
    bluetooth_pairing:
      "true": '{"/api/interfaces/bluetooth": {"pairing": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/interfaces/bluetooth": {"pairing": false}}'
    warning_lens_cap_on:
      "true": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": ["LensCapOn"]}}'
      "false": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": []}}'
    warning_overheating:
      "true": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": ["DeviceOverheating"]}}'
      "false": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": []}}'
    warning_camera_failure:
      "true": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": ["CameraFailure"]}}'
      "false": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": []}}'
    warning_no_device_connected:
      "true": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": ["NoDeviceConnected"]}}'
      "false": '{"/api/device/state": {"warnings": []}}'
    priority_zone_active:
      "true": '{"/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0": {"active": true}}'
      "false": '{"/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0": {"active": false}}'
    beam_azimuth: '{"/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/beam": {"position": {value}}}'
    active_mic: '{"/api/audio/inputs/mixer/activity": {"activeChannel": "{value}"}}'
    max_peak_db: '{"/api/audio/inputs/maxLevel": {"peak": {value}}}'
    mic_peak_db: '{"/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/level": {"peak": {value}}}'
    usb_level_db: '{"/api/audio/inputs/usb": {"level": {value}}}'

  controls:
    - type: select
      key: product
      label: Model
      options: ["TCBarM", "TCBarS"]
    - type: indicator
      key: subscribed_paths
      label: Subscribed Resources
    - type: select
      key: device_state
      label: Device State
      options: ["Normal", "Identifying", "BluetoothPairing", "FirmwareUpdate", "Standby", "CriticalFailure"]
    - type: toggle
      key: identify_active
      label: Identifying
    - type: toggle
      key: user_interaction
      label: User Interaction
    - type: group
      label: "Audio"
      controls:
        - type: toggle
          key: mute
          label: Microphones Muted
        - type: slider
          key: volume
          label: Speaker Volume
          min: 0
          max: 100
          unit: "%"
        - type: slider
          key: beam_azimuth
          label: Talker Azimuth
          min: 15
          max: 165
          unit: "°"
        - type: select
          key: active_mic
          label: Active Microphone
          options: ["InternalMic", "ExternalMic1", "ExternalMic2"]
        - type: toggle
          key: priority_zone_active
          label: Talker in Priority Zone
        - type: slider
          key: mic_peak_db
          label: Microphone Level
          min: -60
          max: 10
          unit: dB
        - type: slider
          key: max_peak_db
          label: Loudest Input Level
          min: -60
          max: 10
          unit: dB
        - type: slider
          key: usb_level_db
          label: USB Input Level
          min: -60
          max: 10
          unit: dB
    - type: group
      label: "Camera"
      controls:
        - type: toggle
          key: camera_active
          label: Camera Active
        - type: toggle
          key: autoframing
          label: Auto Framing
        - type: toggle
          key: person_tiling
          label: Person Tiling
        - type: slider
          key: camera_zoom
          label: Zoom
          min: 100
          max: 500
    - type: group
      label: "Warnings"
      controls:
        - type: toggle
          key: warning_lens_cap_on
          label: Lens Cap On
        - type: toggle
          key: warning_overheating
          label: Overheating
        - type: toggle
          key: warning_camera_failure
          label: Camera Failure
        - type: toggle
          key: warning_no_device_connected
          label: No Device Connected
    - type: toggle
      key: bluetooth_pairing
      label: Bluetooth Pairing

  command_handlers:
    # One dispatcher for every request: the synthesized line is
    # "METHOD /path|body". A matched script handler ends dispatch, so the
    # whole protocol lives in this one block.
    - match: '(?s:.+)'
      handler: |
        def _run():
            line = match.group(0)
            method, _sep, rest = line.partition(" ")
            path, _sep, body = rest.partition("|")
            path = path.split("?")[0]
            data = None
            if body:
                try:
                    data = json.loads(body)
                except ValueError:
                    data = None

            def get(k, default=None):
                return state.get(k, default)

            def is_bar_m():
                return str(get("product", "TCBarM")) != "TCBarS"

            def zoom_ceiling():
                # OpenAPI 1.16, movement.zoomPosition: Bar M Zoom 500,
                # MicrosoftTeams 150, Custom 500; Bar S Zoom 400,
                # MicrosoftTeams 200, Custom 300.
                profile = str(get("device_profile", "Custom"))
                if is_bar_m():
                    return 150 if profile == "MicrosoftTeams" else 500
                if profile == "MicrosoftTeams":
                    return 200
                if profile == "Zoom":
                    return 400
                return 300

            def clamp(v, lo, hi):
                return lo if v < lo else hi if v > hi else v

            # Object resources: path -> ((wire field, state key), ...). The
            # same table answers GETs and applies PUTs.
            FIELDS = {
                "/api/device/site": (("deviceName", "device_name"), ("danteName", "dante_name"),
                                     ("location", "location"), ("position", "position")),
                "/api/device/identification": (("visual", "identify_active"),),
                "/api/firmware/update/state": (("deviceVersion", "firmware_version"), ("state", "update_state"),
                                               ("progress", "update_progress"), ("lastStatus", "update_last_status")),
                "/api/device/hasUserInteraction": (("interaction", "user_interaction"),),
                "/api/device/profile": (("configuration", "device_profile"),),
                "/api/device/allowedStandbyMode": (("mode", "standby_mode"),),
                "/api/device/leds/ring": (("brightness", "led_brightness"),),
                "/api/device/feedback": (("soundPrompts", "sound_prompts"),),
                "/api/device/power/poe/output": (("enabled", "poe_output_enabled"),),
                "/api/interfaces/bluetooth": (("enabled", "bluetooth_enabled"), ("pairing", "bluetooth_pairing"),
                                              ("mac", "bluetooth_mac")),
                "/api/interfaces/network/dante": (("enabled", "dante_enabled"),),
                "/api/interfaces/network/dante/settings": (("continuousDanteStream", "dante_continuous_stream"),
                                                           ("danteSpeakerOutput", "dante_speaker_output")),
                "/api/audio/inputs/mute": (("enabled", "mute"),),
                "/api/audio/outputs/speaker": (("volume", "volume"), ("levelLimiter", "speaker_level_limit")),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic": (("gain", "mic_gain_db"), ("enabled", "mic_enabled")),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate": (("enabled", "noise_gate_enabled"),
                                                            ("threshold", "noise_gate_threshold_db"),
                                                            ("holdTime", "noise_gate_hold_ms"),
                                                            ("range", "noise_gate_range_db")),
                "/api/audio/inputs/noiseSuppression": (("weighting", "noise_suppression"),),
                "/api/audio/soundProfile": (("preset", "sound_profile"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/mixer": (("fadeBehavior", "mixer_fade"),),
                "/api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput": (("farEndGain", "conference_out_far_end_db"),
                                                        ("nearEndGain", "conference_out_near_end_db")),
                "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0": (("gain", "dante_input_1_gain_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1": (("gain", "dante_input_2_gain_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0": (("active", "priority_zone_active"),
                                                                  ("enabled", "priority_zone_enabled"),
                                                                  ("gain", "priority_zone_gain"),
                                                                  ("left", "priority_zone_left"),
                                                                  ("right", "priority_zone_right")),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/beam": (("position", "beam_azimuth"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/mixer/activity": (("activeChannel", "active_mic"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/maxLevel": (("peak", "max_peak_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/level": (("peak", "mic_peak_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/usb": (("level", "usb_level_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/bluetooth": (("level", "bluetooth_level_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0/level": (("value", "dante_input_1_level_db"),),
                "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1/level": (("value", "dante_input_2_level_db"),),
                "/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess": (("autoFramingAccessEnabled", "autoframing_button_enabled"),
                                                             ("autoFramingEnabled", "autoframing"),
                                                             ("personTilingAccessEnabled", "person_tiling_button_enabled"),
                                                             ("personTilingEnabled", "person_tiling")),
                "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement": (("panPosition", "camera_pan"), ("tiltPosition", "camera_tilt"),
                                                             ("zoomPosition", "camera_zoom"), ("zoomSpeed", "camera_zoom_speed"),
                                                             ("panTiltSpeed", "camera_pan_tilt_speed"),
                                                             ("autoFramingSpeed", "autoframing_speed")),
                "/api/video/input/internalCamera": (("active", "camera_active"),),
                "/api/video/input/internalCamera/videoParameters": (("compensation", "camera_compensation"),
                                                                    ("antiFlickerFrequency", "camera_anti_flicker"),
                                                                    ("brightness", "camera_brightness"),
                                                                    ("contrast", "camera_contrast"),
                                                                    ("saturation", "camera_saturation"),
                                                                    ("sharpness", "camera_sharpness"),
                                                                    ("autoWhitebalanceEnabled", "camera_auto_white_balance"),
                                                                    ("whitebalance", "camera_white_balance_k"),
                                                                    ("defaultCameraMode", "camera_default_mode")),
                "/api/video/output/hdmi": (("enabled", "hdmi_enabled"),),
            }
            for z in range(3):
                n = str(z + 1)
                FIELDS["/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/" + str(z)] = (
                    ("active", "exclusion_zone_" + n + "_active"), ("enabled", "exclusion_zone_" + n + "_enabled"),
                    ("left", "exclusion_zone_" + n + "_left"), ("right", "exclusion_zone_" + n + "_right"))

            # What a PUT may change, per resource (the OpenAPI request bodies).
            WRITABLE = {
                "/api/device/identification": ("visual",),
                "/api/device/profile": ("configuration",),
                "/api/device/allowedStandbyMode": ("mode",),
                "/api/device/leds/ring": ("brightness",),
                "/api/device/feedback": ("soundPrompts",),
                "/api/device/power/poe/output": ("enabled",),
                "/api/interfaces/bluetooth": ("enabled", "pairing"),
                "/api/interfaces/network/dante/settings": ("continuousDanteStream", "danteSpeakerOutput"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/mute": ("enabled",),
                "/api/audio/outputs/speaker": ("volume", "levelLimiter"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic": ("gain", "enabled"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/noiseGate": ("enabled", "threshold", "holdTime", "range"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/noiseSuppression": ("weighting",),
                "/api/audio/soundProfile": ("preset",),
                "/api/audio/inputs/mixer": ("fadeBehavior",),
                "/api/audio/outputs/conferenceOutput": ("farEndGain", "nearEndGain"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/dante/0": ("gain",),
                "/api/audio/inputs/dante/1": ("gain",),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0": ("enabled", "gain", "left", "right"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/0": ("enabled", "left", "right"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/1": ("enabled", "left", "right"),
                "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/2": ("enabled", "left", "right"),
                "/api/video/input/internalCamera/aiAccess": ("autoFramingAccessEnabled", "autoFramingEnabled",
                                                             "personTilingAccessEnabled", "personTilingEnabled"),
                "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement": ("panPosition", "tiltPosition", "zoomPosition",
                                                             "zoomSpeed", "panTiltSpeed", "autoFramingSpeed"),
            }

            WARNINGS = (("MicMuted", "warning_mic_muted"), ("LensCapOn", "warning_lens_cap_on"),
                        ("CameraOff", "warning_camera_off"), ("SpeakerMuted", "warning_speaker_muted"),
                        ("NoDeviceConnected", "warning_no_device_connected"),
                        ("DeviceOverheating", "warning_overheating"), ("CpuOverloading", "warning_cpu_overloaded"),
                        ("BluetoothFailure", "warning_bluetooth_failure"), ("DanteFailure", "warning_dante_failure"),
                        ("MicFailure", "warning_mic_failure"), ("SpeakerFailure", "warning_speaker_failure"),
                        ("VoiceEngineFailure", "warning_voice_engine_failure"),
                        ("CameraFailure", "warning_camera_failure"), ("UsbFailure", "warning_usb_failure"),
                        ("TimeUninitialized", "warning_time_uninitialized"),
                        ("NetworkLoopDetected", "warning_network_loop"))

            def hidden():
                return [p for p in str(get("hidden_paths", "")).split(",") if p]

            def eq(prefix):
                return [get(prefix + str(i), 0) for i in range(1, 8)]

            def resource(p):
                """The GET body of one resource path, or None when the bar has no such resource."""
                if p in hidden():
                    return None
                if p in FIELDS:
                    return dict((wire, get(k)) for wire, k in FIELDS[p])
                if p == "/api/device/identity":
                    return {"articleNumber": "700111" if is_bar_m() else "700105",
                            "hardwareRevision": get("hardware_revision"), "product": "TCBarM" if is_bar_m() else "TCBarS",
                            "serial": get("serial"), "vendor": get("vendor")}
                if p == "/api/ssc/version":
                    return {"protocol": get("ssc_protocol_version"), "schema": get("ssc_schema_version")}
                if p == "/api/device/state":
                    return {"state": get("device_state"), "warnings": [w for w, k in WARNINGS if get(k)]}
                if p == "/api/interfaces/network/portConfiguration":
                    conf = str(get("port_configuration", "SingleDomain"))
                    if conf == "Split" and not is_bar_m():
                        conf = "SingleDomain"
                    return {"configuration": conf}
                if p == "/api/interfaces/network/wifi":
                    out = {"enabled": get("wifi_enabled"),
                           "state": "Connected" if get("wifi_connected") else "Disconnected", "connection": {}}
                    if get("wifi_connected"):
                        out["connection"] = {"ssid": get("wifi_ssid"), "security": "WPA/WPA2-Personal",
                                             "signal": get("wifi_signal"), "frequency": get("wifi_band"), "channel": 6}
                    return out
                if p == "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq":
                    return eq("mic_eq_")
                if p == "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq":
                    return eq("speaker_eq_")
                if p == "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones":
                    out = []
                    for z in range(3):
                        b = resource("/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/exclusionZones/" + str(z))
                        b["id"] = z
                        out.append(b)
                    return out
                if p == "/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones":
                    b = resource("/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/priorityZones/0")
                    b["id"] = 0
                    return [b]
                if p == "/api/audio/inputs/dante":
                    return [{"id": 0, "gain": get("dante_input_1_gain_db")}, {"id": 1, "gain": get("dante_input_2_gain_db")}]
                if p == "/api/audio/inputs/dante/levels":
                    return [{"id": 0, "value": get("dante_input_1_level_db")}, {"id": 1, "value": get("dante_input_2_level_db")}]
                return None

            def send(p):
                """One subscription notification: {path: body}."""
                b = resource(p)
                if b is not None:
                    notify(json.dumps({p: b}))

            # ── Subscription session ──
            m = re.match(r"^/api/ssc/state/subscriptions/([0-9a-fA-F-]{36})(/add|/remove)?$", path)
            if m:
                current = [p for p in str(get("subscribed_paths", "")).split(",") if p]
                if method == "DELETE":
                    state["subscribed_paths"] = ""
                    respond("")
                    return
                if method == "GET" and not m.group(2):
                    respond(json.dumps(current))
                    return
                if method == "PUT" and isinstance(data, list):
                    wanted = [str(p) for p in data]
                    if m.group(2) == "/remove":
                        # The whole request is refused when one path is not
                        # subscribed (SSCv2 spec, removing resources).
                        for p in wanted:
                            if p not in current:
                                return
                        state["subscribed_paths"] = ",".join([p for p in current if p not in wanted])
                        respond("")
                        return
                    # A list naming one resource the bar lacks is refused whole.
                    for p in wanted:
                        if resource(p) is None:
                            return
                    if m.group(2) == "/add":
                        new = [p for p in wanted if p not in current]
                        current = current + new
                    else:
                        new = [p for p in wanted if p not in current]
                        current = wanted
                    state["subscribed_paths"] = ",".join(current)
                    for p in new:
                        send(p)
                    respond("")
                    return
                return

            # ── Reads ──
            if method == "GET":
                b = resource(path)
                if b is not None:
                    respond(json.dumps(b))
                return

            if method != "PUT" or path in hidden():
                return

            # ── Commands with no body of their own ──
            if path == "/api/device/restart":
                respond("")
                return
            if path == "/api/video/input/internalCamera/ffov":
                state["camera_pan"] = 0
                state["camera_tilt"] = 0
                state["camera_zoom"] = 100
                respond("")
                send("/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement")
                return
            if path == "/api/video/input/internalCamera/preset/store":
                state["preset_pan"] = get("camera_pan")
                state["preset_tilt"] = get("camera_tilt")
                state["preset_zoom"] = get("camera_zoom")
                respond("")
                return
            if path == "/api/video/input/internalCamera/preset/load":
                state["camera_pan"] = get("preset_pan", 0)
                state["camera_tilt"] = get("preset_tilt", 0)
                state["camera_zoom"] = min(int(get("preset_zoom", 100)), zoom_ceiling())
                respond("")
                send("/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement")
                return

            # ── Seven-band equalizers: the body is the whole array ──
            if path in ("/api/audio/inputs/internalMic/customEq", "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/customEq"):
                if not isinstance(data, list) or len(data) != 7:
                    return
                prefix = "mic_eq_" if "internalMic" in path else "speaker_eq_"
                for i in range(7):
                    state[prefix + str(i + 1)] = clamp(int(data[i]), -8, 8)
                respond("")
                send(path)
                return

            if not isinstance(data, dict):
                return

            # ── Relative moves: by steps, stopping at the end of travel ──
            if path == "/api/audio/outputs/speaker/relative":
                if "volumeUp" in data and "volumeDown" in data:
                    return
                v = int(get("volume", 0)) + int(data.get("volumeUp", 0)) - int(data.get("volumeDown", 0))
                state["volume"] = clamp(v, 0, 100)
                respond("")
                send("/api/audio/outputs/speaker")
                return
            if path == "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement/relative":
                if ("zoomIn" in data and "zoomOut" in data) or ("left" in data and "right" in data) \
                        or ("up" in data and "down" in data):
                    return
                pan = int(get("camera_pan", 0)) + int(data.get("right", 0)) - int(data.get("left", 0))
                tilt = int(get("camera_tilt", 0)) + int(data.get("up", 0)) - int(data.get("down", 0))
                zoom = int(get("camera_zoom", 100)) + int(data.get("zoomIn", 0)) - int(data.get("zoomOut", 0))
                state["camera_pan"] = clamp(pan, -25, 25)
                state["camera_tilt"] = clamp(tilt, -25, 25)
                state["camera_zoom"] = clamp(zoom, 100, zoom_ceiling())
                respond("")
                send("/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement")
                return

            # ── Writes: apply, acknowledge, then notify the whole resource ──
            allowed = WRITABLE.get(path)
            if allowed is None:
                return
            keys = dict(FIELDS[path])
            for wire in allowed:
                if wire in data:
                    state[keys[wire]] = data[wire]
            if path == "/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement":
                state["camera_pan"] = clamp(int(get("camera_pan", 0)), -25, 25)
                state["camera_tilt"] = clamp(int(get("camera_tilt", 0)), -25, 25)
                state["camera_zoom"] = clamp(int(get("camera_zoom", 100)), 100, zoom_ceiling())
            if path == "/api/interfaces/bluetooth" and data.get("enabled") is False:
                # Turning Bluetooth off also ends pairing (OpenAPI 1.16).
                state["bluetooth_pairing"] = False
            respond("")
            send(path)
            if path == "/api/device/profile":
                # A profile change resets the camera settings (and reboots the
                # bar, which the simulator does not); Microsoft Teams also
                # turns the HDMI output off.
                state["camera_pan"] = 0
                state["camera_tilt"] = 0
                state["camera_zoom"] = 100
                state["camera_zoom_speed"] = "Medium"
                state["camera_pan_tilt_speed"] = "Medium"
                state["autoframing_speed"] = "Medium"
                state["hdmi_enabled"] = str(get("device_profile")) != "MicrosoftTeams"
                send("/api/video/input/internalCamera/movement")
                send("/api/video/output/hdmi")

        _run()
